    "created_at": "2025-01-07T08:46:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-07T08:46:13Z",
    "body": "`sequence<BufferSource>` wouldn't serve our use case because it makes a copy of all the data, whereas\r\n\r\n> we explicitly want to allow the function to retain a reference to the passed object, and consume the values produced by the iterable incrementally, to conserve memory.\r\n\r\nIn other words, the differences described [here](https://whatpr.org/webidl/1397.html#idl-async-iterable-type) are important for us (beyond accepting async iterables).\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
